d  shows  well we've been out here for hours and  all i've seen are these stinking loath  cats  additionally this isn't their debut in  the mandalorian either as one variety of  tuka popped up in the season one episode  is sanctuary scaring grogu  unsurprisingly the magistrate can't hold  her own for very long against ahsoka  tano  and ultimately loses their duel the jedi  knocks the spear from her opponent's  hands holding a lightsaber up to her  neck as a form of intimidation  hoping to get the information out of her  that she desires she demands her foe to  reveal the location of grand admiral  thrawn  non-rebels viewers might be a bit lost  here but for those who spend plenty of  time with the ghost crew right up until  the series finale this is exactly the  question they've waited years to find  out the answer to a holdover from the  non-canon star wars expanded universe  grand admiral thrawn burst on the rebel  scene at the beginning of season 3.  during the liberation of lothal at the  end of season four  thrawn and ezra bridger were shot into  hyperspace by a group of purgil  and haven't appeared in any star wars  media since ahsoka and sabine wren  set out to find them shortly after but  as evidenced by the mandalorians reveal  the search goes on at the end of chapter  13  ahsoka doesn't necessarily hold up her  end of the deal once again refusing to  train grogu  but she does give mando a push in the  right direction just before he and his  foundling  board the razer crest for their next  adventure she advises that they set out  for the planet typhon  where the ruins of an ancient jedi  temple reside there grogu can sit on a  seeing stone  and decide between letting his force  abilities go or continuing his long  dormant training you might even be able  to connect with one of the few jedi  left roaming the stars typhon is fairly  new to the star wars universe but it's  important to the overall history of the  galaxy is immense  located in the deep core and